⚙️ Prerequisites & Environment Setup
1. Infrastructure Requirements
The service requires Redis running on localhost:6379. From the repository root:

PowerShell
docker compose up -d
2. Python Virtual Environment Setup
Ensure Python 3.11+ is installed. Navigate to the backend-core directory:

PowerShell
cd backend-core
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
🚀 Running the Services
Testing the distributed execution pipeline requires two terminal processes:

Terminal 1: Celery Background Worker
Starts the task consumer to process agent execution jobs from Redis:

PowerShell
cd backend-core
.\venv\Scripts\activate
celery -A tasks worker --loglevel=info
Terminal 2: Orchestration Controller
Executes the orchestration cycle against the active workers:

PowerShell
cd backend-core
.\venv\Scripts\activate
python orchestrator.py
🧪 Testing
Execute automated unit tests for schemas and round-tracking logic:

PowerShell
pytest test_orchestrator.py
🔌 Team Integration Interfaces
Interface for Member 2 (Consensus Engine)
Hook Location: orchestrator.py -> import evaluate_termination from consensus-engine/scorer.py

Contract: Call evaluate_termination(state.history, state.current_round, state.max_rounds, total_tokens_used) after a round's turns are appended to state.history but before state.current_round is incremented. Returns a TerminationDecision: should_terminate (bool), state (one of converged / partial / stalled / diverging / max_rounds / budget_exceeded / in_progress), consensus_score (float), holdouts (list of dissenting persona names), and message (str). See consensus-engine/README.md for the exact call site and the open item on wiring total_tokens_used through (nothing tracks it yet).

Interface for Member 3 (Model Personas & Prompts)
Hook Location: tasks.py -> execute_agent_turn()

Contract: Replace the mock return payload in execute_agent_turn with real prompt-template execution and LLM inference calls. Must return a dictionary conforming to AgentTurnResult.

Interface for Member 4 (API Service)
Hook Location: orchestrator.py -> initiate_debate()

Contract: Member 4 imports initiate_debate(session_id, query, max_rounds) or dispatches state updates via FastAPI endpoints to start the deliberation flow.


